{"name":"Night Mode","hex":"#234e86","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"night mode","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour scheme with light text and other elements on a dark background."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night_mode"}],"entries":[{"title":"Night Mode (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Night Mode is a Russian sci-fi thriller film directed by Andrey Libenson. It stars Pavel Tabakov and Andrey Merzlikin. This film was theatrically released on August 18, 2022."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Mode_(film)","wikidata":"Q113640819"},{"title":"Dark mode","blocks":[{"text":"A dark mode, dark theme, night mode, or light-on-dark color scheme is a color scheme that uses light-colored text, icons, and graphical user interface elements on a dark background. It is often discussed in terms of computer user interface design and web design. Many modern websites and operating systems offer the user an optional light-on-dark display mode."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Mediawiki-skin-aether.png/330px-Mediawiki-skin-aether.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_mode","wikidata":"Q6545942"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/GNOME_Shell%2C_GNOME_Clocks%2C_Evince%2C_gThumb%2C_GNOME_Files_at_version_3.30_%282018-09%29_in_Dark_theme.png/500px-GNOME_Shell%2C_GNOME_Clocks%2C_Evince%2C_gThumb%2C_GNOME_Files_at_version_3.30_%282018-09%29_in_Dark_theme.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/GNOME_Shell%2C_GNOME_Clocks%2C_Evince%2C_gThumb%2C_GNOME_Files_at_version_3.30_%282018-09%29_in_Dark_theme.png/1280px-GNOME_Shell%2C_GNOME_Clocks%2C_Evince%2C_gThumb%2C_GNOME_Files_at_version_3.30_%282018-09%29_in_Dark_theme.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/GNOME_Shell%2C_GNOME_Clocks%2C_Evince%2C_gThumb%2C_GNOME_Files_at_version_3.30_%282018-09%29_in_Dark_theme.png/500px-GNOME_Shell%2C_GNOME_Clocks%2C_Evince%2C_gThumb%2C_GNOME_Files_at_version_3.30_%282018-09%29_in_Dark_theme.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dark theme for GNOME","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGNOME_Shell%2C_GNOME_Clocks%2C_Evince%2C_gThumb%2C_GNOME_Files_at_version_3.30_(2018-09)_in_Dark